title: Intro
---
///////////////// Play Frisscity calm music track
<<declare $goodend = 0>>
<<declare $badend = 0>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents introLuna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents introLuna lunaNeutral>>
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
Luna: Come on, you stupid SL0P app. Show me the big offers!
<<show SceneSampleEvents introLuna lunaAnnoyed>>
Luna: (Kaya is gonna kill me if I skip out on rent again. Just one big delivery gig should help me break even…)
// SFX cyberdeck notification ping
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents notification>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents introLuna lunaSurprised>>
Luna: (Huh? It's a new customer rating on the SL0P app. I better tap it and check it out…)
<<jump BadReview>>
===




title: BadReview
---
// SFX cyberdeck notification ping
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents notification>>
<<show_notification 0>>
It's a review from the SL0P app, powered by AGENTS. A bad review, too. 
// Show the 1-star review on the screen, which says: “driver didn’t handle with care. my organic belladonna apples were touching the fresh mozzarella and now i can’t eat them anymore cuz i’m a fruitarian vegan going on my 8th juice cleanse.”
<<exit SceneSampleEvents Review>>
////////// We need to remove the asset of Luna leaning on her motorbike before we slide in Luna’s character sprite from the left.
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyed>>
//////////<<expression Luna annoyed>>
Luna: You've got to be joking.
Luna: (I have an option to respond…)


-> Don't respond and close the app
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    Luna: Ugh, whatever.
    I close the app because it isn't worth my time. 
    Frisscity is home to the most privileged people who eat up trends, who crave to act like the city's human augmentation founders and machina millionaires.
    They're freaks. (And they don't tip.) 
    But people like me, from Root Town?
    We refuse to be integrated with AGENTS technology.
    We're all that's left of humanity.
    <<jump CyberdeckTutorial>>
-> Give the reviewer a 1-star rating
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappy>>
    Luna: Heh, shove it.
    I give them a 1-star rating right back, passive-aggressively noting how their fruitarian and vegan preferences weren't mentioned in the app to begin with.
    Luna: That will show them.
    This is the stuff I have to put up with in Frisscity. I break my back for baecoins from the shittiest people alive. 
    I'm waiting for the day everyone finally decides to upload their brains to the cloud.
    If the AGENTS founder does it, I'm sure everyone in Frisscity will follow.     
    But people like me, from Root Town? We'd never fall for a capitalist trick like that.
    We refuse to integrate with AGENTS technology.
    <<jump CyberdeckTutorial>>
-> Doxx their address on an online forum for SL0P drivers
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    Instead of leaving them a 1-star review, I do much worse. I post their address online and warn fellow drivers not to take delivery orders from them. 
    Most of the drivers are from Root Town, where I'm from. Or the Understory, the foggy belly of Frisscity's working class.
    Luna: Now all of SL0P will know what you've done. Good luck getting your stupid apples and cheese. 
    This is the stuff I have to put up with in Frisscity. I break my back for baecoins from the shittiest people alive, who chase trends and chase surgeries to get hooked up with the latest AGENTS technology. 
    But me? I refuse to be augmented.
    I wish Frisscity would just disappear.
    <<jump CyberdeckTutorial>>
===




title: CyberdeckTutorial
---
// SFX cyberdeck notification ping
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents notification>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
Luna: Now what?
<<inspect CyberdeckTutorial>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Tutorial>>
////////////////////////// Populate the cyberdeck. Nat and Luna’s cyberdeck icons should appear as this dialogue progresses. This conversation should happen within the cyberdeck.
<<exit SceneSampleEvents Tutorial>>
<<jump Val>>
===




title: Val
---
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>

Luna: The only thing I need is a big offer so I can get the hell home.
// SFX motorcycle tires
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents tires>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprisedArms>>
I recognize those tires. And the baddie who rides on them.
Luna: (Stay cool.)
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Val>>
Val: Luna! Finally, someone without a corporate T-shirt. Have you been making bank today?
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShyArms>>
Luna: H-Hey, Val. No, not yet. Still getting the low-tipping vegans and high-strung snobs. Y'know how it is.
I hold my breath as Val walks over. She laughs and it's a bright, bubbly sound that goes straight to my heart while her hand goes straight to my head for a gentle pat.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
Val: I'm sure things will turn up by nighttime. All the overworked techies get the late-night munchies.
Luna: (God, she's amazing. She always knows what to say.)
Luna: (But it's kinda weird to see Root Town's corner store queen on this side of town. And so late at night.)
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
Val: Something on your mind?
Luna: (BE. COOL.)
<<jump ValChoices>>
===




title: ValChoices
---
-> Nice bike. How did you mod it? <<once>>
    <<detour Bike_Backstory>>
    <<jump ValChoices>>
-> You look...nice. <<once>>
    <<detour Poor_Flirting>>
    <<jump ValChoices>>
-> What are you doing here?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
    She laughs and gives me a wink.
    Val: A Root Town business never reveals her secrets~!
    <<jump PressingVal>>
===




title: Bike_Backstory
---
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
Val: So, you know how factory models are made for smooth highways, right? B-o-r-i-n-g!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
Val: That's why I reinforced the frame with carbon weave and mag-alloy ribs. Because where we live in Root Town, we need to handle abandoned traincars, vines, and everything in between.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
Val: I cracked my first prototype trying to jump a crumbling overpass!
Luna: (I've unleashed a gearhead beast. There's no end to this conversation.)


->  Let her continue.
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    Val: The engine's got a custom plasma injector, dual cooling loops, and a torque map I programmed myself.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
    Val: Transmission shifts before I even think about it. And the drivetrain is pieced together from three junkyards, one estate auction, and a favor I still owe.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
    Val: But the electrical's my favorite part. Every sensor, every light…I wired those by hand. The original harness was one pothole away from becoming fireworks!
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
    Val: See, that's the thing. Corporate bikes are built to last until the warranty expires.
    Val: But mine's built to survive.She'll outrun anything that's fresh off the showroom floor.
    She rambles on for ten more minutes about the topic. And I love every second of it.
    // Return to the original question node in Val, but remove this question since the player completed it. 
->  Cut it short.
    Luna: I'll hit you up the next time I wanna upgrade my bike. Y'know. For dumb deliveries.
    Val: O-Oh. Of course.
    Val: What did you need again?
    // Return to the original question node in Val, but remove this question since the player completed it. 
===




title: Poor_Flirting
---
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShy>>
Val is beaming, which makes me blush redder than that damn belladonna apple.
Val: That's so sweet! You're cute.
Luna: (C-Cute!?)
Val: But if you think that'll land you a discount at the shop, then you'll need to try harder~
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShyArms>>
Luna: L-Like what?
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
Val: Like getting your hands on a flux ring. They're the first thing to get swiped off a new bike because it's so expensive—and so shiny to the city creatures.
Val: If you get one, I can hook you up with something.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
Val: Something REAL nice~
Luna: !!!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
// Return to the original question node in Val, but remove this question since the player completed it.
===




title: PressingVal
---
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
Past her super good looks and chipper tone, I notice she's a little out of breath. Her eyes shift back to her motorbike.
Luna: (Is she hiding something…?)


-> Ignore it
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    Luna: (It's nothing. She's probably picking up items to take back to her shop.)
    Luna: (Kinda sucks that our town still depends on Frisscity for supplies. But a business is a business, I guess.)
    Val: You're so lost in thought that I'm feeling left out. Let me guess…    
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
    Val: You're thinking about me~?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShyArms>>    
    Luna: W-What!? N-no! Ugh, it's nothing.
    Anything I noticed before has completely vanished.
-> Press her
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    Luna: But your shop's in Root Town. Why do you need to rely on Frisscity to stock your shop? 
    Luna: Or is that the 'secret?'
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valSerious>>
    Val: …
    The silence that washes over us is painful. Something is off.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valFlirty>>
    Val: Boooo, you got me! My glass skin soda pop actually comes from a vendor in Frisscity.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
    Then suddenly she's back to all smiles, like nothing ever happened. It makes me think if what I just experienced was even real.
    Val: You got me! My glass skin soda pop actually comes from a vendor here in the city. 
    Val: I know how divisive that probably sounds to you, but my regulars keep buying it. And when demand is high, well…you gotta feed into it.
<<jump TheOffer>>
===




title: TheOffer
---
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valSerious>>
Val's attention is suddenly stolen by her phone. She smears her thumb across her screen, makes a couple of taps, then hops back onto her motorbike.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Val valNeutral>>
// SFX motorcycle engine turning on
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents engine>>
Val: Sorry, gotta jet! Root Town needs their soda pop.
Val: Stop by tonight, if you're free. I'll be open.
// Val leaves
<<exit SceneSampleEvents Val>>
// SFX motorcycle tires
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents tires>>
Luna: There she goes…
Val is everything I want to be. Independent, spunky. And good with her hands, too.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShyArms>> 
Uh. In the nicest, non-creepiest way possible.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>> 
If it wasn't for my shitty situation, I'd be just like her.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShyArms>> 
Or WITH her? Hm, which is it…?
// SFX cyberdeck notification ping
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents notification>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>> 
Luna: Jackpot.
A big offer on the SL0P app finally lands on my screen.
I quickly accept the offer. It reveals the coordinates of my delivery order's pickup location.
Luna: Time to roll.
// Luna leaves
<<exit SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
// SFX motorcycle engine turning on
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents engine>>
<<wait 2>>
// SFX motorcycle tires
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents tires>>
<<jump TransporterPod>>
===


title: TransporterPod
---
///////////////// Play Frisscity calm music track if it isn’t still already playing
<<background SceneSampleEvents alleyway>>
////////////////// Fade in to show the alleyway environment asset again
<<wait 2>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs podClosed>>
// Show transporter pod asset
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>

<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
Luna: This is…suss.
The pickup location led me into a cramped alleyway. The place reeks of expired seafood scraps and junkyard scrap.
I notice a transporter pod branded with an AGENTS logo sitting by a dumpster. It's an odd place to leave something so brand-spanking new.
////////////////// SFX of something stirring within a metal transporter pod, mixed with alien goober noises
//////////////////<<expression Luna shocked>>
The pod shakes and rolls back and forth on the rubble. Food deliveries don't usually involve grub that's alive.
I hear a distressed noise bellow from within.

-> Put it on the motorcycle
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
    Luna: (I can't just unlock it. That's against SL0P protocol.)
    Luna: (And I can't afford another bad rating. I'd get suspended.)
    I carefully pick up the transporter pod from the ground.
    /////////////////////////// SFX unlock sound
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    But my fingerprints unlock it and bypass the pod's DNA-encoded password security. 
    Which can only mean one thing.
    Luna: (This delivery is…meant for me? But why?)
    Luna: (Why does this pod have my DNA…?)
-> Get closer to inspect it
    <<jump InspectPod>>
-> Kick it around
    <<jump KickPod>>
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
<<jump MeetLilGuy>>
===




title: KickPod
---
<<set $badend += 1>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyed>>
Luna: Fuck AGENTS!
It feels good to stick it to the tech overlords, even if it's just damaging their property. 
The thing inside the pod yelps, but I don't care.
Because everything that AGENTS makes is all the same to me.
Slop.
Other than one scuff, the pod is perfectly intact.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
Luna: (As long as the customer isn't neurotic about how their apples are packaged, then I might just get away with this.)
I pick the transporter pod up.
But when I do…
///////////////// SFX unlock sound
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
My fingerprints unlock it and bypass the pod's DNA-encoded password security.
Which can only mean one thing.
Luna: (This delivery is…meant for me? But why?)
Luna: (Why does this pod have my DNA…?)
And what kind of monster did I just unleash?
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
<<jump MeetLilGuy>>
===




title: InspectPod
---
There's a fingerprint sensor attached to the pod. It's DNA-encoded, which is pretty high security for an underpaid driver like me to be handling.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
???: Free me from this pod, you strange creature!
Luna: (It talks…! But I'M the strange creature?)
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
I glance at the pod's markings again. It's from AGENTS—the very company that's screwed me and humankind over.


-> Unlock the pod
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
    Luna: I can't believe I'm taking orders from a talking pod…
    I'm basically asking for a permanent account suspension—and a possible lawsuit.
    Sighing, I place my hand on the pod's fingerprint sensor.
    Luna: (It's not like the lock won't respond to my biometrics.)
    ///////////////// SFX unlock sound
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    Luna: !!!
    The pod unlocks with my biometric data. Something feels wrong about this whole thing.
    Luna: (This delivery is…meant for me? But why?)
    Luna: (Why does this pod have my DNA…?)
-> Don't unlock it
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>    
    Luna: (I can't just unlock it. That's against SL0P protocol.)
    Luna: (And I can't afford another bad review. I'd get suspended.)
    Luna: (Plus, this thing is from AGENTS. It can't be trusted.)
    ???: Did you not hear me, foreign entity?! I wish to be released. Now!
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
    Luna: I can't. It's against SL0P policy.
    Luna: (Am I really talking to someone's midnight snack?)
    I pick up the transporter pod from the ground, ready to place it on the motorbike and be done with it.
    /////////////////// SFX unlock sound
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    But I wasn't expecting it to unlock with my biometric data. 
    Which can only mean one thing.
    Luna: (This delivery is…meant for me? But why?)
    Luna: (Why does this pod have my DNA…?)
<<jump MeetLilGuy>>
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
===




title: MeetLilGuy
---
///////////////// Play Frisscity calm music track if it isn’t already
// Fade in to show the CG with the transporter pod opened and Lil Guy revealed. Let’s NOT call in character sprites.
<<background SceneSampleEvents lilguyAlleyway>>
<<wait 2>>
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>

The pod sheds its protective packaging and reveals a creature in a large glass container.
It blinks at me from its AGENTS cage, with a screen for a face and pixels for eyes.
It's actually kind of…cute.
???: Ah, so you are not a foreign entity. Just a human. 65% oxygen, 18% carbon, 10% hydrogen, and 3% nitrogen. And with a very concerning crane game addiction.
Luna: And YOU'RE some kinda state-of-the-art cyberpet that talks and scans…body particles?
Luna: (AND scans embarrassing information. Nobody heard that, right?!)
???: I'm not a pet! I'm T.A.B.
Luna: Tab…?
???: Technologically Advanced Broseph. Fit for the future of all bro-kind. My name's origin stems from a company naming event.
???: I could not just be called “bro.” It needed to be more technical, more SEO-optimized. And so my name was keyword-stuffed to absolute perfection.
Luna: (I'm literally losing brain cells talking to this thing…)
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
<<jump LilGuyReaction>>
===




title: LilGuyReaction
---
<<background SceneSampleEvents alleyway>>
// Now we’re back to the alleyway environment background asset with regular character sprites
///////////////// Play Frisscity calm music track if it isn’t already playing
<<wait 2>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs podNeutral>>
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>


// If player chose to Kick it around, show:
<<if visited("KickPod") == true>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs podAngry>>
    T.A.B: How dare you kick a perfect high-fidelity prototype like me around!
    <<exit SceneSampleEvents Nubs podAngry>>
    The creature crawls out of the pod to give me a piece of its mind. The circuits in its tadpole-like tail jolt to life.
    <<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngryWave>> 
    T.A.B: My master will have your head for this! As well as the AGENTS Legal team! When they get their hands on that pod’s sensor—
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
    Luna: Whoa, hold up. I'm not the one that tossed you here like trash. I'm just the delivery girl. Also…
    I shove the transporter pod into the dumpster, which smears it with unspeakable leftovers. I give it one last push, and the glass on the fingerprint sensor cracks, erasing traces of my DNA in the process.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna armsHappy>>
    Luna: What sensor?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs angry>> 
    T.A.B: …
    Luna: AGENTS tech is pretty fragile, huh? Not as ‘high-fidelity’ as it claims to be.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna armsNeutral>>
    Luna: Now, as for you…
<<endif>>
//If else, show:
<<if visited("KickPod") == false>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna armsNeutral>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs podNeutral>>
    T.A.B: So you eventually came to your senses. You realized that stealing intellectual property from the most powerful corporation in Area 415 was wrong and costly. You have my thanks.
    <<exit SceneSampleEvents Nubs podNeutral>>
    <<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
    The creature slowly emerges from the pod. 
    A curious tadpole-like tail swishes from side to side.
    Luna: (Meh. The face was cuter.)
    T.A.B: As for my master, well. He will thank you with damage fees and lawsuits within the next 1-2 business days.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    Luna: W-Wait, hold up! “Stealing?” I'm just the delivery girl. I didn't toss you here like trash!
    The creature waves his tiny nubs at the transporter pod.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngryWavey>>
    T.A.B: It's too late! This AGENTS pod sensor has already captured your DNA, which can and will be used against you in the court of law.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
    Luna: Oh yeah?
    I immediately shove the transporter pod into the dumpster and smear its sensor with unspeakable leftovers.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappy>>
    Luna: Oops! There goes my DNA.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
    T.A.B: Ah. 
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsLoading>>
    T.A.B: Recalculating potential lawsuit probability to 15%.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: Let's keep it that way. 
    Luna: (Time to cross-examine this alien.)
<<endif>>
<<jump LilGuyQuestions>>
===




title: LilGuyQuestions
---
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
-> What are you? <<once>>
    <<detour WhatAreYou>>
    <<jump LilGuyQuestions>>
    // Return to the original questions in LilGuyQuestions node, but remove this question since the player completed it.
